    feat(ward-flow): the statistics section skeleton, and the constant gap named on the page
    
    TWO AGENTS' WORK IN ONE COMMIT, DELIBERATELY. Both were finished and neither could
    commit: the pre-commit hook refuses when a staged change triggers a generator and other
    working-tree files are inputs to that same generator, and each held files the other's
    generator reads. Sequencing was impossible, so the alternatives were --no-verify (which
    left aa97b92a1 with stale generated docs earlier today), a stash (forbidden — the stack is
    shared across worktrees), or one agent's work landing under the other's message. This is
    the only option that keeps the generated docs honest and attributes both.
    
    Cost, stated plainly: the two changes are less independently revertible than two commits
    would have been.
    
    --- The skeleton (13 files) ---
    
    Four new routes under /mockups/ward-flow/statistics: overview (across all services and
    Western Australia), compare (ward and ED comparisons), and dynamic ward/[unitId] and
    ed/[edId] for one unit in detail. One shared statistics-sections.ts holds each section's
    id, href and description so the hub index and the tests read the same fact.
    
    Nothing shows an invented figure. Each section states what it will hold and that it is not
    built — never a nought, never a dash standing where a number will go, because a figure
    that looks measured is worse than a blank when nobody re-checks a number that renders. A
    test asserts the placeholders contain no numeral at all.
    
    The dynamic screens refuse to fall back to another unit when an id does not resolve: a
    page showing the wrong ward under the right heading is worse than a page showing nothing.
    
    --- The constant gap named on the page (2 files) ---
    
    The arrival average showed one number as its average, its shortest and its longest,
    because the admissions fixture derives one instant from the other by a fixed offset. The
    page now says so, but only when the two ends meet AND more than one admission was
    measured, and it distinguishes what it can see (the ends coincide) from why (an
    explanation the shape points at, not a finding the page established). It disappears on its
    own the moment the gaps differ. No digit appears in the copy, asserted by a test.
    
    --- docs/site-map.md ---
    
    Regenerated by the hook, and it adds FIVE routes, not four. /mockups/ward-flow/statistics
    itself had never been in the site map: aa97b92a1 was committed with --no-verify while a
    scratch file blocked the hook, so the generator never ran for it. That gap closes here.
    
    --- Evidence ---
    
    tsc -p tsconfig.typecheck.json --noEmit: exit 0.
    vitest over the five disk-discovered tests/ward-statistics* files: 100 passed (100).
    eslint and prettier clean over all 13 new files.
    
    Both agents proved their load-bearing assertions can fail, by mutation, restoring each
    file with a matching hash: inserting a numeral into the overview copy turned the numeral
    assertions red; making the ward screen fall back to units[0] turned the not-found test
    red; removing the measured-count guard turned exactly the single-admission test red while
    the spread test stayed green.
    
